<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stefan Nemanja</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1113–1199</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Saint Simeon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stefan Nemanja was Grand Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> from about 1166 to 1196 and founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nemanjic-dynasty">Nemanjić dynasty</a>. He united the Serbian lands, conquering Duklja and Zachlumia, and won independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> in practice. He abdicated to become the monk Simeon and with his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sava">Sava</a> founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hilandar">Hilandar</a> monastery on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-athos">Mount Athos</a>; he is venerated as a saint.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stefan-nemanja.jpg" alt="Stefan Nemanja" width="320" height="472" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stefan_Nemanja.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
